Z||000000||Ali_Gulf_Fiero||11-08-2001||04:24 PM||||I have an '85 Sport Coupe with the 5sp Isuzu. It had the clutch replaced recently. What I would like you gents in-the-know to let me know is what the correct pedal travel should be, and where the engagement curve should be. What determines this? I've driven Fieros where the clutch is fully engaged only a couple of inches off the floor. Mine the engagement is from a half-inch off the floor to the top of release. Is this a function of wear in the former instance, and adjustable in the second? I'd like a bit less travel for full engagement. I'm guessing at the nomenclature guys; I hope y'all follow my line of questioning!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I'm editing this cuz my friend just told me to get off my lazy arse and search the topic. Sorry for flogging a dead horse; it's the only horse I have, and it's a cute horse!<BR>Still, I'd be oh-so grateful if you'd put a smidge of input into this post. Thanksabunch!<P><BR>------------------<BR>my cat's sitting in my scrambled eggs.<p>[This message has been edited by Ali_Gulf_Fiero (edited 11-08-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||11-08-2001||04:52 PM||||That's a tad long on the throw - sounds like you still have air in the system. Check out all the different bleeding procedures via the search.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MrPBody||11-08-2001||08:15 PM||||That does sound unusual.  My '85 SE 2.5 engages fully about 1/3 up from the floor.  I'm guesstimating of course because I can't simultaneously measure and drive.<BR>||||reg||1
